  "content": {
    "id": "p51-q13-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "13",
    "prompt": "A particle is projected from a point O with speed $34\\text{ m/s}$ at angle $\\theta$ above the horizontal.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p51-q13-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that the parabolic path has equation $$y=x\\tan\\theta-\\frac{5x^2\\sec^2\\theta}{1156}.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=x\\tan\\theta-\\dfrac{5x^2\\sec^2\\theta}{1156}$.",
          "worked": "Using the Cartesian projectile equation with $g=10\\text{ m/s}^2$ and $V=34\\text{ m/s}$, \n\n$$\\begin{aligned}y&=x\\tan\\theta-\\frac{gx^2}{2V^2}\\sec^2\\theta\\\\y&=x\\tan\\theta-\\frac{10x^2}{2(34^2)}\\sec^2\\theta\\\\y&=x\\tan\\theta-\\frac{5x^2\\sec^2\\theta}{1156}.\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 21
      },
      {
        "id": "p51-q13-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "The particle passes through a point $11\\text{ m}$ above O and $30\\text{ m}$ horizontally from O.\n\nShow that the two possible angles of projection are $\\theta=\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\dfrac{8}{15}\\right)$ and $\\theta=\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\dfrac{538}{75}\\right)$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\dfrac{8}{15}\\right)$ or $\\theta=\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\dfrac{538}{75}\\right)$.",
          "worked": "At $(30,11)$, let $\\tau=\\tan\\theta$, so $\\sec^2\\theta=1+\\tau^2$. \n\n$$\\begin{aligned}11&=30\\tau-\\frac{4500}{1156}(1+\\tau^2)\\\\11&=30\\tau-\\frac{1125}{289}(1+\\tau^2)\\\\3179&=8670\\tau-1125(1+\\tau^2)\\\\1125\\tau^2-8670\\tau+4304&=0\\\\\\tau&=\\frac{8670\\pm\\sqrt{8670^2-4(1125)(4304)}}{2250}\\\\\\tau&=\\frac{8670\\pm7470}{2250}\\\\\\tau&=\\frac{538}{75}\\quad\\text{or}\\quad\\frac{8}{15}.\\end{aligned}$$\n\n Therefore $\\theta=\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\dfrac{8}{15}\\right)$ or $\\theta=\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\dfrac{538}{75}\\right)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 49
      }
    ]
  },
